<h2 id="intersection-section-cycle-of-closed" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0AZA">43.4</span> Cycle associated to closed subscheme</h2>

<p>
Suppose that $X$ is a variety and that $Z \subset X$ be a closed subscheme with $\dim (Z) \leq k$. Let $Z_ i$ be the irreducible components of $Z$ of dimension $k$ and let $n_ i$ be the <em>multiplicity of $Z_ i$ in $Z$</em> defined as 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  n_ i = \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, Z_ i}} \mathcal{O}_{Z, Z_ i}  \]
</div>
<p>
 where $\mathcal{O}_{X, Z_ i}$, resp. $\mathcal{O}_{Z, Z_ i}$ is the local ring of $X$, resp. $Z$ at the generic point of $Z_ i$. We define the $k$-cycle associated to $Z$ to be the $k$-cycle 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  [Z]_ k = \sum n_ i [Z_ i].  \]
</div>
<p>
 See Chow Homology, Section <a href="/tag/02QS" data-tag="02QS">42.9</a>. 
</p>
